STORIES_LOAD("jo",{"jo1":{"passage":[[1,1,14]],"intro":[{"sc":"cosmos","n":"John begins his Gospel just like Genesis: \"In the beginning...\""},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"\"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God. He was with God in the beginning. Through Him all things were made; without Him nothing was made that has been made.\""},{"sc":"starsky","n":"\"In Him was life, and that life was the light of all people. The light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.\""},{"sc":"nativity","n":"\"He came to that which was His own, but His own did not receive Him. Yet to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God.\""},{"sc":"nativity","n":"\"The Word became flesh and made His dwelling among us. We have seen His glory, the glory of the one and only Son, who came from the Father, full of grace and truth.\""},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"🔎 Did you know? Why does John call Jesus 'the Word'? Words show what's in someone's heart and mind. Jesus is God's perfect 'Word': when we look at Jesus, we see exactly what God is like. And the Word who spoke the universe into being in Genesis 1 became a baby!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God moved into the neighbourhood","text":"The One who made the stars became a human being and lived among us. 'Made His dwelling' literally means 'pitched His tent', like the tabernacle in the desert. God didn't just send a message; He came Himself. And everyone who receives Him becomes a child of God."},"order":["\"In the beginning was the Word\"","The Word was God","All things were made through Him","The light shines in the darkness","Those who receive Him become God's children","The Word became flesh"],"quiz":[{"q":"How does John's Gospel begin?","o":["In the beginning was the Word","A baby was born","There was a king","Once upon a time"],"why":"John 1:1."},{"q":"What did the Word become?","o":["Flesh, a human being","A book","A star","A king of Rome"],"why":"John 1:14."},{"q":"What can the darkness not do to the light?","o":["Overcome it","See it","Hear it","Find it"],"why":"John 1:5."}],"words":["WORD","LIGHT","FLESH","GLORY","GRACE","TRUTH"]},"jo2":{"passage":[[1,29,42]],"intro":[{"sc":"jordan","n":"The next day John the Baptist saw Jesus coming towards him."},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjohnb","e":"big","t":"Look, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!"},{"sc":"jordan","n":"The next day John was there again with two of his disciples. When he saw Jesus passing by, he said again, \"Look, the Lamb of God!\" When the two disciples heard this, they followed Jesus."},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"What do you want?"},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bandrew","e":"smile","t":"Rabbi, where are You staying?"},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come, and you will see."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"They spent the day with Him. One of the two was Andrew. The first thing Andrew did was find his brother Simon and tell him, \"We have found the Messiah!\" And he brought him to Jesus."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"📜 Promise kept: 'The Lamb of God': remember Abraham telling Isaac, 'God Himself will provide the lamb' (Genesis 22:8)? And the Passover lambs in Egypt? And Isaiah's Servant 'led like a lamb' (Isaiah 53:7)? John the Baptist pointed to Jesus: here He is!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Bring someone to Jesus","text":"The first thing Andrew did after meeting Jesus was find his brother and bring him to Jesus. Andrew never became as famous as Peter, but without Andrew, Peter might never have met Jesus! Leaders bring others to Jesus, starting with their own family."},"order":["John sees Jesus coming","\"Look, the Lamb of God!\"","Two disciples follow Jesus","\"Come, and you will see\"","Andrew finds his brother Simon","\"We have found the Messiah!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did John the Baptist call Jesus?","o":["The Lamb of God","The Lion of Judah","The King","The Teacher"],"why":"John 1:29."},{"q":"Who did Andrew bring to Jesus?","o":["His brother Simon","His mother","His friend Philip","Nobody"],"why":"John 1:41-42."},{"q":"What did Jesus say when asked where He was staying?","o":["Come, and you will see","Go away","It's a secret","Nowhere"],"why":"John 1:39."}],"words":["LAMB","ANDREW","MESSIAH","FOLLOW","BROTHER","FOUND"]},"jo3":{"passage":[[1,43,51]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"The next day Jesus decided to leave for Galilee. Finding Philip, He said to him, \"Follow Me.\""},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bphilip","e":"big","t":"Nathanael! We've found the one Moses wrote about in the Law, and the prophets wrote about too: Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph!"},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bnathanael","e":"smirk","t":"Nazareth! Can anything good come from there?"},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bphilip","e":"smile","t":"Come and see."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Here truly is an Israelite in whom there is nothing false."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bnathanael","e":"shock","t":"How do You know me?"},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I saw you while you were still under the fig tree, before Philip called you."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"bnathanael","e":"big","t":"Rabbi, You are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!"},{"sc":"figtree","n":"🔎 Did you know? Nazareth was a tiny, unimportant village, never mentioned in the Old Testament. Nathanael was being honest about his doubts! Philip didn't argue. He just said, 'Come and see.' That's still the best answer to doubters."}],"lesson":{"title":"Come and see","text":"Nathanael was honest: he doubted. Philip didn't argue or get offended; he invited: 'Come and see.' And when Nathanael met Jesus, he discovered Jesus already knew him. Leaders don't win arguments; they invite people to meet Jesus for themselves."},"order":["Jesus calls Philip","Philip finds Nathanael","\"Can anything good come from Nazareth?\"","\"Come and see\"","\"I saw you under the fig tree\"","\"You are the Son of God!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Nathanael say about Nazareth?","o":["Can anything good come from there?","It's beautiful","It's my home","Nothing"],"why":"John 1:46."},{"q":"What was Philip's answer?","o":["Come and see","You're wrong","Be quiet","I don't know"],"why":"John 1:46."},{"q":"Where had Jesus 'seen' Nathanael?","o":["Under the fig tree","In the temple","On a boat","In the market"],"why":"John 1:48."}],"words":["NATHANAEL","PHILIP","NAZARETH","COME","SEE","FIGTREE"]},"jo4":{"passage":[[2,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"wedding","n":"There was a wedding in Cana in Galilee. Jesus' mother was there, and Jesus and His disciples had also been invited."},{"sc":"wedding","n":"Weddings lasted a whole week! But halfway through, the wine ran out. In those days, that would be a terrible embarrassment for the family."},{"sc":"wedding","w":"bmary","e":"worried","t":"They have no more wine."},{"sc":"wedding","n":"Then Mary said to the servants:"},{"sc":"wedding","w":"bmary","e":"smile","t":"Do whatever He tells you."},{"sc":"wedding","n":"Nearby stood six large stone water jars, each holding 80 to 120 litres. Jesus said to the servants, \"Fill the jars with water.\" So they filled them to the brim."},{"sc":"wedding","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Now draw some out and take it to the master of the banquet."},{"sc":"wedding","n":"The master of the banquet tasted the water, which had become wine! He called the bridegroom: \"Everyone brings out the best wine first, and the cheaper wine later. But you have saved the best till now!\" This was the first of Jesus' signs, and His disciples believed in Him."}],"lesson":{"title":"Do whatever He tells you","text":"Mary's words to the servants are the best advice in the Bible: 'Do whatever He tells you.' The servants filled the jars with water, which didn't make sense, but they obeyed, and saw the miracle. And Jesus' first sign was at a party, saving a family from embarrassment. He cares about our joys too."},"order":["A wedding in Cana","The wine runs out","Mary tells Jesus","\"Do whatever He tells you\"","The servants fill six jars with water","The water becomes the best wine"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was the wedding?","o":["Cana in Galilee","Jerusalem","Bethlehem","Nazareth"],"why":"John 2:1."},{"q":"What did Mary tell the servants?","o":["Do whatever He tells you","Go home","Buy more wine","Be quiet"],"why":"John 2:5."},{"q":"How many stone jars were there?","o":["Six","Two","Twelve","One"],"why":"John 2:6."}],"words":["WEDDING","CANA","WATER","WINE","JARS","SIGN"]},"jo5":{"passage":[[3,1,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"There was a Pharisee named Nicodemus, a member of the Jewish ruling council. He came to Jesus at night, maybe so no one would see him."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bnicodemus","e":"smile","t":"Rabbi, we know You are a teacher who has come from God. No one could do the signs You are doing if God were not with Him."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Very truly I tell you, no one can see the kingdom of God unless they are born again."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bnicodemus","e":"worried","t":"How can someone be born when they are old? Surely they can't go back into their mother's womb!"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"No one can enter the kingdom of God unless they are born of water and the Spirit. The wind blows wherever it pleases. You hear its sound, but can't tell where it comes from or where it's going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that whoever believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life. For God did not send His Son into the world to condemn the world, but to save the world through Him."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"🔎 Did you know? John 3:16 is probably the most famous verse in the Bible. It has been called 'the Gospel in a nutshell': God's love, God's gift, our response, and the result, all in one sentence!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Born again","text":"Nicodemus was a respected teacher who knew the Scriptures well. But Jesus told him he needed a completely new start: a new birth by God's Spirit. Being good and religious isn't enough. Everyone needs to receive God's gift of new life. 'For God so loved the world... whoever believes.'"},"order":["Nicodemus comes to Jesus at night","\"You are a teacher from God\"","\"You must be born again\"","\"How can someone be born when old?\"","The Spirit is like the wind","\"For God so loved the world\""],"quiz":[{"q":"When did Nicodemus come to Jesus?","o":["At night","At noon","At dawn","On a feast day"],"why":"John 3:2."},{"q":"What did Jesus say a person must be?","o":["Born again","Rich","Old","A priest"],"why":"John 3:3."},{"q":"What did Jesus compare the Spirit to?","o":["The wind","Fire","Water only","A dove"],"why":"John 3:8."}],"words":["NICODEMUS","NIGHT","BORN","AGAIN","SPIRIT","LOVED"]},"jo6":{"passage":[[4,5,30],[4,39,42]],"intro":[{"sc":"well","n":"Jesus was travelling through Samaria. Tired from the journey, He sat down by Jacob's well. It was about noon, the hottest part of the day."},{"sc":"well","n":"A Samaritan woman came to draw water. Women usually came in the cool of the morning. Maybe she came at noon to avoid people."},{"sc":"well","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Will you give Me a drink?"},{"sc":"well","w":"bsamwoman","e":"shock","t":"You're a Jew and I'm a Samaritan woman. How can You ask me for a drink?"},{"sc":"well","n":"Jews didn't talk to Samaritans, and a Jewish teacher wouldn't talk to a woman alone. But Jesus did!"},{"sc":"well","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"If you knew the gift of God and who it is that asks you for a drink, you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water. Everyone who drinks this water will be thirsty again, but whoever drinks the water I give will never thirst."},{"sc":"well","n":"Jesus told her things about her life that only God could know: she'd had five husbands, and was now living with someone who wasn't her husband. Yet He still offered her living water. \"I know the Messiah is coming,\" she said. Jesus answered, \"I, the one speaking to you, am He.\""},{"sc":"well","n":"She left her water jar, ran back to town, and told everyone: \"Come, see a man who told me everything I ever did! Could this be the Messiah?\" Many Samaritans believed in Jesus because of her words."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus knows everything, and still offers living water","text":"Jesus broke three rules to talk to her: a Jew to a Samaritan, a man to a woman, a teacher to someone with a messy life. He knew everything about her, and still offered her the gift of living water. She went from hiding to telling her whole town. Leaders talk to people others avoid."},"order":["Jesus sits by Jacob's well at noon","A Samaritan woman comes for water","\"Will you give Me a drink?\"","Jesus offers living water","He tells her about her life","She brings her whole town to Jesus"],"quiz":[{"q":"Whose well did Jesus sit beside?","o":["Jacob's","David's","Abraham's","Moses'"],"why":"John 4:6."},{"q":"What did Jesus offer the woman?","o":["Living water","Money","Bread","A new jar"],"why":"John 4:10."},{"q":"What did she leave behind when she ran to town?","o":["Her water jar","Her cloak","Her sandals","Her friend"],"why":"John 4:28."}],"words":["WELL","LIVING","WATER","THIRST","SAMARIA","MESSIAH"]},"jo7":{"passage":[[4,46,54]],"intro":[{"sc":"wedding","n":"Jesus visited Cana in Galilee again, where He had turned water into wine."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"A royal official, an important man from the king's court, came from Capernaum, about 30 km away. His son was close to death."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bofficial","e":"worried","t":"Sir, come down before my child dies!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go. Your son will live."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"The man took Jesus at His word and set off for home. He didn't argue or insist Jesus come with him. He believed and went."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"While he was still on the way, his servants met him with the news that his boy was alive! \"When did he get better?\" \"Yesterday, at one in the afternoon, the fever left him.\""},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"The father realised that was the exact time Jesus had said, \"Your son will live.\" So he and his whole household believed."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jesus healed the boy from 30 km away, without seeing or touching him! It was the second of seven 'signs' in John's Gospel. Each sign shows something about who Jesus is."}],"lesson":{"title":"Take Jesus at His word","text":"The official wanted Jesus to come with him. Jesus just said, 'Go, your son will live.' And the man believed Him and went home, without seeing anything yet. Faith means trusting what Jesus says, even before we see the result. Leaders take Jesus at His word."},"order":["Jesus is in Cana again","A royal official's son is dying","\"Come before my child dies!\"","\"Go. Your son will live\"","The man believes and goes","His son recovered at that exact hour"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus tell the official?","o":["Go. Your son will live","I'll come with you","Wait here","Bring him to Me"],"why":"John 4:50."},{"q":"What did the man do?","o":["Took Jesus at His word and went home","Argued","Stayed","Cried"],"why":"John 4:50."},{"q":"When did the boy get better?","o":["At the exact time Jesus spoke","A week later","The next morning","Never"],"why":"John 4:53."}],"words":["OFFICIAL","WORD","BELIEVE","SON","HEALED","DISTANCE"]},"jo8":{"passage":[[5,1,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"pool","n":"In Jerusalem, near the Sheep Gate, was a pool called Bethesda, surrounded by five covered porches. Lying there were a great number of disabled people: the blind, the lame, the paralysed."},{"sc":"pool","n":"One man there had been unable to walk for thirty-eight years. That's longer than most people's parents have been alive!"},{"sc":"pool","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Do you want to get well?"},{"sc":"pool","w":"bpoolman","e":"worried","t":"Sir, I have no one to help me into the pool when the water is stirred. While I'm trying to get in, someone else goes down ahead of me."},{"sc":"pool","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Get up! Pick up your mat and walk."},{"sc":"pool","n":"At once the man was cured. He picked up his mat and walked!"},{"sc":"pool","n":"But it was the Sabbath, and some leaders were more upset that he was carrying his mat than glad that he'd been healed after 38 years!"},{"sc":"pool","n":"🔎 Did you know? Archaeologists have actually found the Pool of Bethesda in Jerusalem, with the remains of its five porches, exactly as John described!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Do you want to get well?","text":"Jesus' question seems strange: of course he wanted to be well! But after 38 years, maybe he'd given up hope, and all he could think about was who would help him. Jesus didn't need the pool. Leaders bring hope to people who've given up, and don't let rules get in the way of joy."},"order":["The Pool of Bethesda has five porches","A man has been ill for 38 years","\"Do you want to get well?\"","\"I have no one to help me\"","\"Get up! Pick up your mat and walk\"","He walks, on the Sabbath"],"quiz":[{"q":"How long had the man been unable to walk?","o":["Thirty-eight years","Three days","Eight years","Forty days"],"why":"John 5:5."},{"q":"What was the pool called?","o":["Bethesda","Siloam","Jordan","Galilee"],"why":"John 5:2."},{"q":"What has been discovered about the pool?","o":["Archaeologists found it, with five porches","It never existed","It's under the sea","Nothing"],"why":"John 5:2."}],"words":["POOL","BETHESDA","MAT","WALK","WAITED","HOPE"]},"jo9":{"passage":[[6,5,14],[6,35,35],[6,66,69]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"A huge crowd had followed Jesus up a mountainside. Jesus asked Philip, \"Where shall we buy bread for these people to eat?\" (He already knew what He was going to do.)"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bandrew","e":"worried","t":"Here is a boy with five small barley loaves and two small fish. But how far will they go among so many?"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bboylunch","e":"smile","t":"You can have my lunch!"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Jesus took the loaves, gave thanks, and handed them out to everyone, as much as they wanted. Five thousand men were fed, and twelve baskets of leftovers were collected! Barley loaves were the cheapest bread, food for poor people. A poor boy's lunch fed a crowd."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to Me will never go hungry, and whoever believes in Me will never be thirsty."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Later, many of His followers found His teaching too hard and turned back. Jesus asked the twelve, \"You don't want to leave too, do you?\""},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"Lord, to whom shall we go? You have the words of eternal life."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"✨ \"I am\": This is the first of Jesus' seven great 'I am' sayings in John. When God spoke to Moses at the burning bush, He said His name was 'I AM' (Exodus 3:14). Each time Jesus says 'I am...', He's showing who He is."}],"lesson":{"title":"Bring your lunch to Jesus","text":"Only John tells us the loaves came from a boy. He didn't have much, but he gave what he had, and Jesus fed thousands with it. And Jesus Himself is the bread that satisfies our deepest hunger. Young people: what you offer Jesus can make a huge difference."},"order":["A huge crowd needs food","Andrew finds a boy with five loaves and two fish","The boy gives his lunch","Jesus feeds five thousand","\"I am the bread of life\"","\"Lord, to whom shall we go?\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who gave the five loaves and two fish?","o":["A boy","Peter","A baker","A rich man"],"why":"John 6:9."},{"q":"What kind of loaves were they?","o":["Barley, the cheapest bread","Wheat","Honey cakes","Rye"],"why":"John 6:9."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He is?","o":["The bread of life","A baker","A farmer","A fisherman"],"why":"John 6:35."}],"words":["BREAD","LIFE","BOY","LOAVES","BARLEY","HUNGRY"]},"jo10":{"passage":[[8,2,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"At dawn, Jesus was teaching in the temple courts, with crowds gathered around Him."},{"sc":"temple","n":"The teachers of the law and the Pharisees brought in a woman who had been caught doing something wrong, something the law of Moses said deserved death by stoning. They made her stand in front of everyone."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bpharisee","e":"smirk","t":"Teacher, this woman was caught breaking the law. Moses commanded us to stone such women. Now what do You say?"},{"sc":"temple","n":"It was a trap. If Jesus said 'Let her go', they'd say He disobeyed Moses. If He said 'Stone her', He'd lose His reputation for mercy, and break Roman law. Jesus bent down and started to write on the ground with His finger."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Let any one of you who is without sin be the first to throw a stone at her."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Again He bent down and wrote on the ground. At this, those who heard began to go away one at a time, the older ones first, until only Jesus was left, with the woman still standing there."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Woman, where are they? Has no one condemned you?"},{"sc":"temple","w":"bwomancaught","e":"worried","t":"No one, sir."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Then neither do I condemn you. Go now and leave your life of sin."}],"lesson":{"title":"Mercy, and a new start","text":"Everyone was ready to throw stones. Jesus made them look at their own hearts, and they all walked away. Then He did two things: He refused to condemn her, and He told her to change. Jesus offers both forgiveness and a new life. Leaders don't throw stones; they offer mercy and a fresh start."},"order":["Leaders bring a woman to Jesus","\"Moses said to stone her\"","Jesus writes on the ground","\"Let anyone without sin throw the first stone\"","They leave one by one","\"Neither do I condemn you; go and sin no more\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus do while they questioned Him?","o":["Wrote on the ground with His finger","Shouted","Walked away","Picked up a stone"],"why":"John 8:6."},{"q":"Who left first?","o":["The older ones","The youngest","The woman","Jesus"],"why":"John 8:9."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to the woman?","o":["Neither do I condemn you; go and sin no more","You're guilty","Run!","Nothing"],"why":"John 8:11."}],"words":["STONES","MERCY","CONDEMN","WROTE","FORGIVE","NEWSTART"]},"jo11":{"passage":[[8,12,12],[9,1,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"I am the light of the world. Whoever follows Me will never walk in darkness, but will have the light of life."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"As Jesus went along, He saw a man who had been blind from birth. His disciples asked, \"Rabbi, who sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?\""},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Neither this man nor his parents sinned. This happened so that the works of God might be displayed in him. While I am in the world, I am the light of the world."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Then Jesus spat on the ground, made some mud with the saliva, and put it on the man's eyes. \"Go, wash in the Pool of Siloam.\""},{"sc":"pool","n":"So the man went and washed, and came home seeing! For the first time in his life, he saw colours, faces, the sky!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"His neighbours couldn't believe it. \"Isn't this the man who used to sit and beg?\" Some said yes; others said it just looked like him. He kept saying, \"I am the man!\""},{"sc":"pool","n":"✨ \"I am\": 'I am the Light of the World' is Jesus' second 'I am' saying. And He proved it by giving light to the eyes of a man who had never seen any light at all."}],"lesson":{"title":"Not anyone's fault","text":"The disciples wanted someone to blame for the man's blindness. Jesus said: stop looking for blame; look for what God can do. Leaders don't assume people's troubles are their own fault. They look for ways God can show His goodness through them."},"order":["\"I am the light of the world\"","A man has been blind from birth","\"Who sinned?\"","\"Neither; God's works will be shown\"","Jesus puts mud on his eyes","He washes in Siloam and sees"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jesus send the blind man to wash?","o":["The Pool of Siloam","The Jordan","The sea","Bethesda"],"why":"John 9:7."},{"q":"What did Jesus put on the man's eyes?","o":["Mud made with saliva","Oil","Water","A cloth"],"why":"John 9:6."},{"q":"Whose fault did Jesus say the blindness was?","o":["Nobody's","The man's","His parents'","The priests'"],"why":"John 9:3."}],"words":["LIGHT","BLIND","MUD","SILOAM","SEE","WORLD"]},"jo12":{"passage":[[9,13,38]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"The healed man was brought to the Pharisees. Jesus had made mud on the Sabbath, which they said was 'work'! They questioned him, then his parents."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"His parents were afraid of being thrown out of the synagogue. \"He's our son, and he was born blind. But how he can see now, we don't know. Ask him. He's old enough.\""},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bpharisee","e":"frown","t":"Give glory to God! We know this man Jesus is a sinner!"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bblindman","e":"big","t":"Whether He's a sinner or not, I don't know. One thing I do know: I was blind, but now I see!"},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"They kept questioning him. He got bolder: \"I've told you already! Do you want to become His disciples too? If this man were not from God, He could do nothing!\" So they threw him out."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Jesus heard they had thrown him out, and went and found him. \"Do you believe in the Son of Man?\" \"Who is He, sir? Tell me so that I may believe in Him.\" \"You have now seen Him; in fact, He is the one speaking with you.\""},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bblindman","e":"big","t":"Lord, I believe!"},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'I was blind, but now I see' became one of the most famous lines in the world, in the hymn 'Amazing Grace', written by John Newton, a former slave-ship captain who became a Christian and later fought against the slave trade."}],"lesson":{"title":"Tell what you know","text":"The man didn't know all the answers to the experts' questions. But he knew his own story: 'I was blind, but now I see!' He stood firm even when he was thrown out, and Jesus came looking for him. Leaders tell honestly what Jesus has done for them, even when they can't answer every question."},"order":["The Pharisees question the healed man","His parents are afraid","\"This man is a sinner!\"","\"I was blind, but now I see!\"","They throw him out","Jesus finds him: \"Lord, I believe!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the man say he knew for sure?","o":["I was blind, but now I see","Jesus is a sinner","Nothing","The Pharisees are right"],"why":"John 9:25."},{"q":"What did the Pharisees do to him?","o":["Threw him out","Gave him a reward","Made him a priest","Ignored him"],"why":"John 9:34."},{"q":"Which famous hymn uses his words?","o":["Amazing Grace","Silent Night","Jesus Loves Me","Joy to the World"],"why":"John Newton's hymn."}],"words":["BLIND","SEE","AMAZING","GRACE","BELIEVE","BOLD"]},"jo13":{"passage":[[10,7,16],[10,27,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I am the gate for the sheep. Whoever enters through Me will be saved. They will come in and go out, and find pasture."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy. I have come that they may have life, and have it to the full."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep. The hired hand isn't the shepherd and doesn't own the sheep. So when he sees the wolf coming, he abandons the sheep and runs away."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I am the good shepherd; I know My sheep and My sheep know Me. My sheep listen to My voice; I know them, and they follow Me."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"I give them eternal life, and they shall never perish. No one will snatch them out of My hand."},{"sc":"field","n":"🔎 Did you know? In those days, shepherds often brought several flocks into one sheepfold at night. In the morning, each shepherd called, and only his own sheep came, because they knew his voice. Even today, shepherds in the Middle East and Africa do the same!"},{"sc":"field","n":"✨ \"I am\": Two 'I am' sayings: 'I am the Gate' and 'I am the Good Shepherd'. Remember Psalm 23, 'The Lord is my shepherd'? And Ezekiel 34, where God promised to come and shepherd His people Himself? Here He is."}],"lesson":{"title":"Know His voice","text":"Jesus isn't a hired worker who runs away when danger comes. He's the Good Shepherd who knows each sheep by name, and gave His life for them. His sheep learn to recognise His voice. Leaders listen for Jesus' voice in His word, and follow Him."},"order":["\"I am the gate for the sheep\"","\"I have come to give life to the full\"","\"I am the good shepherd\"","The hired hand runs from the wolf","\"My sheep know My voice\"","\"No one will snatch them out of My hand\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the good shepherd do for the sheep?","o":["Lays down his life for them","Sells them","Runs away","Ignores them"],"why":"John 10:11."},{"q":"What does the hired hand do when the wolf comes?","o":["Runs away","Fights","Calls for help","Hides the sheep"],"why":"John 10:12."},{"q":"How do the sheep know their shepherd?","o":["By his voice","By his clothes","By his smell","By his staff"],"why":"John 10:4, 27."}],"words":["SHEPHERD","SHEEP","VOICE","GATE","WOLF","LIFE"]},"jo14":{"passage":[[11,1,6],[11,17,37]],"intro":[{"sc":"hut","n":"Jesus loved Martha, her sister Mary, and their brother Lazarus, in the village of Bethany. One day the sisters sent Him a message: \"Lord, the one You love is sick.\""},{"sc":"hut","n":"Strangely, when Jesus heard this, He stayed where He was for two more days. He knew something they didn't."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"When Jesus finally arrived, Lazarus had already been in the tomb for four days. Martha ran out to meet Him."},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bmartha","e":"worried","t":"Lord, if You had been here, my brother wouldn't have died."},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Your brother will rise again. I am the resurrection and the life. The one who believes in Me will live, even though they die. Do you believe this?"},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bmartha","e":"smile","t":"Yes, Lord. I believe that You are the Messiah, the Son of God."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Then Mary came, fell at His feet, weeping, and said the same thing. When Jesus saw her weeping, and the people with her weeping too, He was deeply moved and troubled."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"\"Where have you laid him?\" \"Come and see, Lord.\" And Jesus wept."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"✨ \"I am\": 'I am the Resurrection and the Life' is Jesus' fifth 'I am' saying. And 'Jesus wept' is the shortest verse in most English Bibles: just two words. Jesus knew He was about to raise Lazarus, and He still wept with His friends."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus cries with you","text":"Jesus knew He would raise Lazarus in a few minutes. But He still wept with Mary and Martha in their grief. He doesn't rush past our sadness. When you're hurting, Jesus understands and cares. Leaders weep with those who weep, and don't hurry them past their pain."},"order":["Lazarus is sick","Jesus waits two days","Lazarus has been dead four days","\"I am the resurrection and the life\"","Mary weeps at His feet","Jesus wept"],"quiz":[{"q":"How long had Lazarus been in the tomb?","o":["Four days","One day","A week","A year"],"why":"John 11:17."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He is?","o":["The resurrection and the life","A doctor","A prophet","A gardener"],"why":"John 11:25."},{"q":"What is the shortest verse in most English Bibles?","o":["Jesus wept","God is love","Pray always","Rejoice always"],"why":"John 11:35."}],"words":["LAZARUS","WEPT","MARTHA","RISE","BETHANY","BELIEVE"]},"jo15":{"passage":[[11,38,45]],"intro":[{"sc":"tomb","n":"Jesus, once more deeply moved, came to the tomb. It was a cave with a stone laid across the entrance."},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Take away the stone."},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bmartha","e":"worried","t":"But, Lord, by this time there will be a bad smell. He's been there four days!"},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Didn't I tell you that if you believe, you will see the glory of God?"},{"sc":"tomb","n":"So they took away the stone. Jesus looked up and prayed: \"Father, I thank You that You have heard Me.\""},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Lazarus, come out!"},{"sc":"tomb","n":"And the dead man came out, his hands and feet wrapped with strips of linen, and a cloth around his face!"},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Take off the grave clothes and let him go."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Many of the people who had come to visit Mary, and had seen what Jesus did, believed in Him."}],"lesson":{"title":"Nothing is too dead for Jesus","text":"Four days dead, a stone across the tomb, and a bad smell: completely hopeless. But Jesus called, and Lazarus walked out. Then Jesus asked the people to help unwrap him. Jesus brings new life; and He invites us to help others get free from what still binds them."},"order":["Jesus comes to the tomb","\"Take away the stone\"","\"There will be a bad smell!\"","Jesus thanks the Father","\"Lazarus, come out!\"","\"Take off the grave clothes\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Martha worry about when Jesus said to remove the stone?","o":["The smell","The guards","The weight","Nothing"],"why":"John 11:39."},{"q":"What did Jesus shout?","o":["Lazarus, come out!","Wake up!","Goodbye!","Help!"],"why":"John 11:43."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell the people to do?","o":["Take off the grave clothes and let him go","Run away","Close the tomb","Nothing"],"why":"John 11:44."}],"words":["LAZARUS","COMEOUT","STONE","TOMB","LINEN","GLORY"]},"jo16":{"passage":[[12,20,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"Some Greeks, foreigners, came to Jerusalem to worship at the festival. They came to Philip with a request: \"Sir, we would like to see Jesus.\""},{"sc":"temple","n":"Philip told Andrew, and Andrew and Philip told Jesus."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The hour has come for the Son of Man to be glorified. Very truly I tell you, unless a kernel of wheat falls to the ground and dies, it remains only a single seed. But if it dies, it produces many seeds."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Anyone who loves their life will lose it, while anyone who hates their life in this world will keep it for eternal life. Whoever serves Me must follow Me; and where I am, My servant also will be."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Now My soul is troubled, and what shall I say? 'Father, save Me from this hour'? No, it was for this very reason I came. Father, glorify Your name!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Then a voice came from heaven: \"I have glorified it, and will glorify it again.\""},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"🔎 Did you know? One wheat seed planted in the ground can produce a plant with dozens of new seeds! Jesus was explaining that His death would bring life to millions of people from every nation, like those Greeks who wanted to see Him."}],"lesson":{"title":"Giving your life produces fruit","text":"A seed kept in your pocket stays a single seed. Planted in the ground, it 'dies', and grows into many. Jesus' death would bring life to the whole world. Leaders give their lives away in serving others, and that's how their lives bear fruit."},"order":["Greeks want to see Jesus","Philip and Andrew tell Jesus","\"The hour has come\"","\"Unless a seed falls and dies...\"","\"It produces many seeds\"","A voice from heaven answers"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who wanted to see Jesus?","o":["Some Greeks","Romans","Egyptians","Babylonians"],"why":"John 12:20-21."},{"q":"What does a seed do if it dies?","o":["Produces many seeds","Disappears","Turns to stone","Nothing"],"why":"John 12:24."},{"q":"What came from heaven?","o":["A voice","Fire","Rain","Manna"],"why":"John 12:28."}],"words":["SEED","WHEAT","GREEKS","FRUIT","GLORIFY","HOUR"]},"jo17":{"passage":[[13,1,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"It was just before the Passover. Jesus knew His time had come to leave this world. Having loved His own, He now showed them the full extent of His love."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"In those days people walked on dusty roads in sandals, and a servant usually washed the guests' dirty feet. But there was no servant there. And none of the disciples offered to do it."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"So Jesus got up from the meal, took off His outer clothing, and wrapped a towel around His waist. He poured water into a basin, and began to wash His disciples' feet, drying them with the towel."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bpeter","e":"shock","t":"Lord, are You going to wash MY feet? No, You shall never wash my feet!"},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Unless I wash you, you have no part with Me."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bpeter","e":"big","t":"Then, Lord, not just my feet, but my hands and my head as well!"},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Do you understand what I have done for you? You call Me 'Teacher' and 'Lord', and rightly so. Now that I, your Lord and Teacher, have washed your feet, you also should wash one another's feet. I have set you an example. Now that you know these things, you will be blessed if you do them."}],"lesson":{"title":"The King with a towel","text":"The Lord of the universe knelt down with a towel and a basin and did the dirtiest servant's job, washing twelve pairs of dusty feet, including Judas's! This is what leadership looks like in Jesus' kingdom. Leaders take the lowest jobs, and serve others gladly."},"order":["No servant is there to wash feet","Jesus takes a towel and basin","He washes the disciples' feet","Peter refuses at first","\"Not just my feet, but all of me!\"","\"I have set you an example\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus wrap around His waist?","o":["A towel","A rope","A belt","A cloak"],"why":"John 13:4."},{"q":"Who refused at first to have his feet washed?","o":["Peter","John","Judas","Thomas"],"why":"John 13:8."},{"q":"What did Jesus say we should do for one another?","o":["Wash one another's feet, and serve","Argue","Ignore each other","Be served"],"why":"John 13:14."}],"words":["TOWEL","BASIN","FEET","WASH","SERVE","EXAMPLE"]},"jo18":{"passage":[[13,34,35],[14,1,9]],"intro":[{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"A new command I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you must love one another. By this everyone will know that you are My disciples, if you love one another."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"The disciples were worried. Jesus had told them He was going away. What would they do without Him?"},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe also in Me. My Father's house has many rooms. I am going there to prepare a place for you. And I will come back and take you to be with Me."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bthomas","e":"worried","t":"Lord, we don't know where You are going, so how can we know the way?"},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bphilip","e":"worried","t":"Lord, show us the Father, and that will be enough for us."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't you know Me, Philip, even after I have been among you such a long time? Anyone who has seen Me has seen the Father."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"✨ \"I am\": 'I am the Way, the Truth and the Life' is the sixth 'I am' saying. Thomas asked for directions, and Jesus said, 'I am the directions!' He doesn't just show the way to God; He IS the way."}],"lesson":{"title":"Love is the badge","text":"Jesus said people would know His followers not by their clothes, songs or buildings, but by how they love one another. And when we're worried about the future, He says: don't be troubled, I'm preparing a place for you, and I am the Way. Leaders are known for their love."},"order":["\"Love one another as I have loved you\"","\"By this all will know you are My disciples\"","\"Don't let your hearts be troubled\"","\"I'm preparing a place for you\"","\"I am the way, the truth and the life\"","\"Whoever has seen Me has seen the Father\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How will everyone know we are Jesus' disciples?","o":["If we love one another","By our clothes","By our money","By our buildings"],"why":"John 13:35."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He is?","o":["The way, the truth and the life","A road","A door only","A teacher only"],"why":"John 14:6."},{"q":"Who asked, 'How can we know the way?'","o":["Thomas","Peter","Judas","John"],"why":"John 14:5."}],"words":["WAY","TRUTH","LIFE","LOVE","TROUBLED","PLACE"]},"jo19":{"passage":[[15,1,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"vineyard","n":"Perhaps walking past vineyards on the way to Gethsemane, Jesus gave His final 'I am' saying."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I am the true vine, and My Father is the gardener. He cuts off every branch in Me that bears no fruit, and every branch that does bear fruit He prunes, so that it will be even more fruitful."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Remain in Me, as I also remain in you. No branch can bear fruit by itself; it must remain in the vine. Neither can you bear fruit unless you remain in Me."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"I am the vine; you are the branches. If you remain in Me and I in you, you will bear much fruit. Apart from Me you can do nothing."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Greater love has no one than this: to lay down one's life for one's friends. You are My friends if you do what I command. I no longer call you servants. Instead, I have called you friends."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"✨ \"I am\": 'I am the Vine' is the seventh 'I am' saying. Remember Isaiah's song of the vineyard, and Israel as God's vine? Jesus is the 'true vine', and everyone joined to Him becomes a branch that bears fruit."}],"lesson":{"title":"Stay connected","text":"A branch cut off from the vine can't grow a single grape, no matter how hard it tries. Its job is to stay connected. Fruit grows naturally. Stay close to Jesus every day, in prayer, His word and His people, and fruit will grow in your life. And Jesus calls you His friend!"},"order":["\"I am the true vine\"","\"My Father is the gardener\"","\"Remain in Me\"","\"Apart from Me you can do nothing\"","\"Greater love has no one than this\"","\"I have called you friends\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who is the gardener?","o":["The Father","Jesus","Peter","Moses"],"why":"John 15:1."},{"q":"What happens to branches that stay in the vine?","o":["They bear much fruit","They wither","They break","Nothing"],"why":"John 15:5."},{"q":"What does Jesus call His followers?","o":["Friends","Servants only","Strangers","Workers"],"why":"John 15:15."}],"words":["VINE","BRANCHES","FRUIT","REMAIN","FRIENDS","GARDENER"]},"jo20":{"passage":[[17,1,3],[17,20,26]],"intro":[{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"After talking with His disciples, Jesus looked up towards heaven and prayed. It's the longest prayer of Jesus in the Bible."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Father, the hour has come. Glorify Your Son, that Your Son may glorify You. Now this is eternal life: that they know You, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom You have sent."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"He prayed for His disciples, that the Father would protect them. And then He prayed for someone else..."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"My prayer is not for them alone. I pray also for those who will believe in Me through their message..."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"That's you! Everyone who would ever believe in Jesus because of the apostles' message, in every country and every century, including you, right now."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"...that all of them may be one, Father, just as You are in Me and I am in You. May they also be in Us, so that the world may believe that You have sent Me."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jesus' prayer for His followers to be united is especially meaningful in Africa, where Christians from many tribes, languages and churches worship the same Lord. Our unity shows the world who Jesus is."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus prayed for you, by name","text":"The night before He died, Jesus prayed for you: for everyone who would believe through the apostles' message. And His prayer was that we'd be united. Leaders work for unity among Christians from different churches, tribes and backgrounds."},"order":["Jesus looks up to heaven and prays","\"This is eternal life: to know You\"","He prays for His disciples","He prays for future believers","That includes you!","\"That they may be one\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Jesus pray for besides His disciples?","o":["Those who would believe through their message","Only Himself","Only the priests","Nobody else"],"why":"John 17:20."},{"q":"What is eternal life, according to Jesus?","o":["Knowing the only true God and Jesus Christ","Living forever on earth","Being rich","Being good"],"why":"John 17:3."},{"q":"What did Jesus pray His followers would be?","o":["One, united","Rich","Famous","Strong"],"why":"John 17:21."}],"words":["PRAYER","ONE","UNITY","KNOW","BELIEVE","GLORY"]},"jo21":{"passage":[[18,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"Jesus went with His disciples across the Kidron Valley to an olive garden. Judas came there, guiding a detachment of soldiers and officials, carrying torches, lanterns and weapons."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Who is it you want?"},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"\"Jesus of Nazareth.\" Jesus said, \"I am He.\" When Jesus said 'I am He', they drew back and fell to the ground!"},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"Then Simon Peter, who had a sword, drew it and struck the high priest's servant, cutting off his right ear. The servant's name was Malchus."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Put your sword away! Shall I not drink the cup the Father has given Me?"},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"Luke the doctor adds that Jesus touched the man's ear and healed him (Luke 22:51). Jesus' last miracle before the cross was healing an enemy who had come to arrest Him!"},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"🔎 Did you know? Only John tells us the servant's name: Malchus. Maybe John knew him, because John knew the high priest's household (John 18:15). Did Malchus ever forget the man who healed his ear on the night He was arrested?"}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus heals even His enemies","text":"Peter tried to fight with a sword. Jesus stopped him, and healed the man who'd come to arrest Him. Jesus wasn't a victim; the soldiers fell back at His word! He chose to go to the cross. Leaders don't fight evil with violence; they answer with love, even to their enemies."},"order":["Judas leads soldiers to the garden","\"Who is it you want?\"","\"I am He,\" and they fall back","Peter cuts off Malchus's ear","\"Put your sword away!\"","Jesus heals the ear"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the high priest's servant called?","o":["Malchus","Barabbas","Lazarus","Judas"],"why":"John 18:10."},{"q":"What happened when Jesus said 'I am He'?","o":["The soldiers drew back and fell to the ground","They laughed","They ran","Nothing"],"why":"John 18:6."},{"q":"What did Jesus do to the servant's ear?","o":["Healed it","Ignored it","Covered it","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 22:51."}],"words":["MALCHUS","SWORD","EAR","HEALED","ENEMY","GARDEN"]},"jo22":{"passage":[[18,33,38],[19,1,6],[19,12,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Early in the morning, they led Jesus to the palace of the Roman governor, Pontius Pilate."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpilate","e":"stern","t":"Are You the king of the Jews?"},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"My kingdom is not of this world. If it were, My servants would fight. You say that I am a king. In fact, the reason I was born and came into the world is to testify to the truth. Everyone on the side of truth listens to Me."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpilate","e":"smirk","t":"What is truth?"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Pilate went out to the crowd: \"I find no basis for a charge against Him.\" He had Jesus whipped, and the soldiers twisted a crown of thorns and put a purple robe on Him. Pilate brought Him out: \"Here is the man!\""},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"But the chief priests and officials shouted, \"Crucify! Crucify!\" Three times Pilate said He was innocent. But the crowd shouted, \"If you let this man go, you are no friend of Caesar!\""},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Afraid of losing his position, Pilate sat on the judge's seat, and handed Jesus over to be crucified."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"🔎 Did you know? Pilate asked 'What is truth?' while Truth Himself was standing right in front of him! Just hours earlier, Jesus had said, 'I am the Way, the Truth and the Life.'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Stand for truth, whatever it costs","text":"Pilate knew Jesus was innocent; he said so three times. But he cared more about keeping his job and pleasing the crowd than doing what was right. Leaders do what's right even when it's unpopular and costly, and don't hide behind 'What is truth?'"},"order":["Jesus is taken to Pilate","\"Are You the king of the Jews?\"","\"My kingdom is not of this world\"","\"What is truth?\"","Pilate says three times: He is innocent","Pilate hands Him over to be crucified"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Pilate ask Jesus about truth?","o":["What is truth?","Where is truth?","Who has truth?","Nothing"],"why":"John 18:38."},{"q":"How many times did Pilate say Jesus was innocent?","o":["Three","Once","Seven","Never"],"why":"John 18:38; 19:4, 6."},{"q":"Why did Pilate hand Jesus over?","o":["He was afraid of losing favour with Caesar and the crowd","Jesus was guilty","He hated Jesus","Jesus asked him to"],"why":"John 19:12."}],"words":["PILATE","TRUTH","KINGDOM","INNOCENT","CROWD","THORNS"]},"jo23":{"passage":[[19,16,19],[19,25,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Carrying His own cross, Jesus went out to the place of the Skull, called Golgotha. There they crucified Him, with two others, one on each side. Pilate had a sign fastened to the cross in three languages: JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Near the cross stood His mother Mary, His mother's sister, Mary the wife of Clopas, and Mary Magdalene. And John, the disciple whom He loved."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Woman, here is your son."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Here is your mother."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"From that time on, John took Mary into his home and cared for her. Even dying on the cross, Jesus made sure His mother would be looked after."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Knowing that everything had now been finished, so that Scripture would be fulfilled, Jesus said, \"I am thirsty.\" They put a sponge soaked in sour wine on a hyssop stalk and lifted it to His lips."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"It is finished."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"With that, He bowed His head and gave up His spirit."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'It is finished' is just one word in Greek: 'tetelestai'. It was written on receipts when a debt was paid in full. Jesus wasn't saying 'I'm finished'; He was saying 'It's done! The debt is paid!'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Paid in full","text":"On the cross, Jesus still cared for His mother. And His final cry was a shout of victory: 'It is finished!', the debt paid in full. There's nothing left for us to pay. We simply receive what He finished. Leaders live as people whose debt has been completely paid."},"order":["Jesus carries His cross to Golgotha","The sign: King of the Jews, in three languages","Mary and John stand near the cross","\"Here is your mother\"","\"I am thirsty\"","\"It is finished\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Jesus ask to care for His mother?","o":["John, the disciple He loved","Peter","Thomas","Pilate"],"why":"John 19:26-27."},{"q":"What were Jesus' last words in John's Gospel?","o":["It is finished","Help Me","Goodbye","Father, forgive them"],"why":"John 19:30."},{"q":"What does 'tetelestai' mean on a receipt?","o":["Paid in full","Late","Cancelled","Pending"],"why":"It is finished."}],"words":["FINISHED","CROSS","MOTHER","THIRSTY","PAID","VICTORY"]},"jo24":{"passage":[[19,38,42]],"intro":[{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Joseph of Arimathea had been a disciple of Jesus, but secretly, because he was afraid of the Jewish leaders. Now he went to Pilate and asked for Jesus' body."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"He was accompanied by Nicodemus, the man who had first come to Jesus at night!"},{"sc":"tomb","w":"bnicodemus","e":"worried","t":"I've brought spices: myrrh and aloes. About thirty-four kilograms."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Thirty-four kilograms of spices! That was enough for a king's burial. Nicodemus, who had once come secretly in the dark, now openly honoured Jesus in the daylight, when it was most dangerous."},{"sc":"garden","n":"At the place where Jesus was crucified there was a garden, and in the garden a new tomb, in which no one had ever been laid. They wrapped Jesus' body with the spices in strips of linen, and laid Him there."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"🔎 Did you know? Remember the wise men's gift of myrrh at Jesus' birth? Myrrh was used for burial. Jesus received myrrh at the beginning of His life and at the end."}],"lesson":{"title":"From secret to open","text":"Joseph and Nicodemus had been secret followers, afraid of what others would think. But when Jesus died, when it was most dangerous, they stepped out publicly. Sometimes faith takes time to grow brave. Leaders stop hiding their faith and honour Jesus openly."},"order":["Joseph of Arimathea asks for Jesus' body","He had been a secret disciple","Nicodemus comes too","He brings 34 kg of spices","They wrap the body in linen","They lay Jesus in a new tomb in a garden"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who came with Joseph of Arimathea?","o":["Nicodemus","Peter","Thomas","Pilate"],"why":"John 19:39."},{"q":"How much spice did Nicodemus bring?","o":["About 34 kg","A small jar","None","1 kg"],"why":"John 19:39."},{"q":"Where was the tomb?","o":["In a garden","On a mountain","In the city","By the sea"],"why":"John 19:41."}],"words":["NICODEMUS","JOSEPH","SPICES","MYRRH","GARDEN","BRAVE"]},"jo25":{"passage":[[20,1,18]],"intro":[{"sc":"garden","n":"Early on the first day of the week, while it was still dark, Mary Magdalene went to the tomb and saw that the stone had been removed! She ran to Peter and John: \"They have taken the Lord out of the tomb, and we don't know where they have put Him!\""},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Peter and John ran to the tomb. John, younger and faster, got there first. They saw the strips of linen lying there, and the face cloth folded up by itself. John saw and believed. Then they went home."},{"sc":"garden","n":"But Mary stood outside the tomb, crying. Two angels asked her, \"Woman, why are you crying?\" \"They have taken my Lord away.\" Then she turned around and saw Jesus standing there, but she didn't recognise Him."},{"sc":"garden","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Woman, why are you crying? Who is it you are looking for?"},{"sc":"garden","w":"bmarym","e":"worried","t":"Sir, if you have carried Him away, tell me where you have put Him, and I will get Him."},{"sc":"garden","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Mary."},{"sc":"garden","w":"bmarym","e":"big","t":"Rabboni! (Teacher!)"},{"sc":"garden","n":"Jesus sent her to tell the others. Mary Magdalene went to the disciples with the news: \"I have seen the Lord!\""},{"sc":"garden","n":"🔎 Did you know? Remember the Song of Solomon episode, 'Seeking the One I Love'? The church fathers connected it with this very moment: a woman searching in the dark, and finding the One her heart loved in a garden."}],"lesson":{"title":"He knows your name","text":"Mary was so heartbroken she didn't recognise Jesus, until He said one word: her name. The first person Jesus appeared to after rising was a woman whose life He had transformed. Jesus knows you by name too. And like Mary, we're sent to say: 'I have seen the Lord!'"},"order":["Mary finds the stone removed","Peter and John run to the tomb","Mary stays, weeping","She thinks Jesus is the gardener","Jesus says, \"Mary\"","\"I have seen the Lord!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Mary think Jesus was at first?","o":["The gardener","An angel","Peter","A soldier"],"why":"John 20:15."},{"q":"What made Mary recognise Jesus?","o":["He said her name","She saw His hands","He sang","He touched her"],"why":"John 20:16."},{"q":"What did Mary tell the disciples?","o":["I have seen the Lord!","He's gone","I'm scared","Nothing"],"why":"John 20:18."}],"words":["MARY","GARDEN","RABBONI","NAME","RISEN","SEEN"]},"jo26":{"passage":[[20,19,31]],"intro":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"On the evening of that first day, the disciples were together, with the doors locked for fear of the Jewish leaders. Jesus came and stood among them!"},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Peace be with you! As the Father has sent Me, I am sending you. Receive the Holy Spirit."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"But Thomas wasn't there. When the others told him, \"We have seen the Lord!\", he said:"},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bthomas","e":"frown","t":"Unless I see the nail marks in His hands and put my finger where the nails were, and put my hand into His side, I will not believe."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"A week later, the disciples were in the house again, and Thomas was with them. The doors were locked, but Jesus came and stood among them: \"Peace be with you!\""},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Thomas, put your finger here; see My hands. Reach out your hand and put it into My side. Stop doubting and believe."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bthomas","e":"big","t":"My Lord and my God!"},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Because you have seen Me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not seen and yet have believed."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"John writes: \"These are written that you may believe that Jesus is the Messiah, the Son of God, and that by believing you may have life in His name.\" That's why this whole Gospel was written: for you!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Honest doubts, and a great confession","text":"Thomas was honest about his doubts. Jesus didn't scold him; He came back, especially for him, and showed him the scars. And Thomas made the greatest confession in the Gospels: 'My Lord and my God!' Then Jesus blessed us: all who believe without seeing. Bring your honest questions to Jesus."},"order":["Jesus appears behind locked doors","\"Peace be with you\"","Thomas isn't there","\"Unless I see the nail marks...\"","Jesus shows Thomas His hands","\"My Lord and my God!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Thomas want to see?","o":["The nail marks in Jesus' hands","An angel","The empty tomb","A miracle"],"why":"John 20:25."},{"q":"What did Thomas say when he saw Jesus?","o":["My Lord and my God!","I still don't believe","Hello","Who are You?"],"why":"John 20:28."},{"q":"Who did Jesus call blessed?","o":["Those who have not seen and yet have believed","Only Thomas","Only the disciples","Nobody"],"why":"John 20:29."}],"words":["THOMAS","DOUBT","BELIEVE","HANDS","PEACE","LORD"]},"jo27":{"passage":[[21,1,14]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"Later, some of the disciples were by the Sea of Galilee. Simon Peter said, \"I'm going fishing.\" \"We'll go with you.\" They went out in the boat, but that night they caught nothing."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"Early in the morning, Jesus stood on the shore, but the disciples didn't realise it was Jesus. \"Friends, haven't you any fish?\" \"No.\""},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Throw your net on the right side of the boat and you will find some."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"When they did, they couldn't haul the net in because of the huge number of fish! Then John said to Peter, \"It is the Lord!\""},{"sc":"galilee","n":"As soon as Peter heard that, he wrapped his outer garment around him and jumped into the water, swimming to shore! The others followed in the boat, towing the net full of fish."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"When they landed, they saw a fire of burning coals there, with fish on it, and some bread. Jesus had made them breakfast!"},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Bring some of the fish you have just caught. Come and have breakfast."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"The net held 153 large fish, and it didn't tear! Jesus took the bread and gave it to them, and did the same with the fish."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"🔎 Did you know? This is just like the day Peter first met Jesus, when they'd fished all night, caught nothing, and then filled their nets (Luke 5)! Jesus was taking Peter back to where it all began."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus cooks breakfast","text":"The risen Lord of the universe stood on a beach at dawn, cooking fish for His tired friends. He didn't scold them for going back to fishing. He met them where they were, fed them and called them back. Leaders care for people's practical needs, not just their spiritual ones."},"order":["The disciples fish all night and catch nothing","A stranger on the shore says, \"Try the right side\"","The net is full","\"It is the Lord!\"","Peter jumps into the water","Jesus has made breakfast"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many fish were in the net?","o":["153","12","1,000","5"],"why":"John 21:11."},{"q":"What did Peter do when he realised it was Jesus?","o":["Jumped into the water","Hid","Kept fishing","Fell asleep"],"why":"John 21:7."},{"q":"What had Jesus prepared on the beach?","o":["Breakfast of fish and bread","A boat","A tent","Nothing"],"why":"John 21:9."}],"words":["BREAKFAST","BEACH","FISH","NET","FIRE","DAWN"]},"jo28":{"passage":[[21,15,19],[21,24,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"beachfire","n":"When they had finished eating, Jesus turned to Peter. Peter, who had denied Him three times beside a charcoal fire. Now they sat beside another charcoal fire."},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Simon son of John, do you love Me more than these?"},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"Yes, Lord, You know that I love You."},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Feed My lambs."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"Jesus asked a second time, \"Do you love Me?\" \"Yes, Lord, You know I love You.\" \"Take care of My sheep.\""},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"The third time Jesus said, \"Simon, do you love Me?\" Peter was hurt because Jesus asked him the third time."},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"Lord, You know all things; You know that I love You."},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Feed My sheep. Follow Me!"},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"John ends his Gospel: \"Jesus did many other things as well. If every one of them were written down, I suppose that even the whole world would not have room for the books that would be written.\""},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"🔎 Did you know? Three denials, three questions, three restorations. Jesus didn't just forgive Peter privately; He gave him a job: 'Feed My sheep.' Peter went on to lead the early church, preach at Pentecost, and write two letters in the Bible."}],"lesson":{"title":"Love Him, and feed His sheep","text":"Peter had failed three times. Jesus asked three times, 'Do you love Me?', not to shame him, but to heal him, one question for each denial. Then He gave him a job: look after My people. Failure isn't the end. Jesus restores us and sends us to serve. Do you love Him?"},"order":["Breakfast by a charcoal fire","\"Do you love Me?\"","\"Feed My lambs\"","Asked three times","Peter is hurt: \"You know all things\"","\"Feed My sheep. Follow Me!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How many times did Jesus ask Peter, 'Do you love Me?'","o":["Three","Once","Seven","Twice"],"why":"John 21:17."},{"q":"What job did Jesus give Peter?","o":["Feed My sheep","Go fishing","Build a temple","Write a book"],"why":"John 21:17."},{"q":"Why three times?","o":["Once for each time Peter had denied Him","Jesus forgot","Peter didn't hear","No reason"],"why":"Three denials, three restorations."}],"words":["LOVE","FEED","SHEEP","LAMBS","RESTORED","FOLLOW"]}});
